     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Peter- It&#39;s true. That&#39;s why I led off with &quot;This question may be a little out of place here&quot;.<div><br></div><div>Quoting the ggvis page at rstudio, <i>&quot;The graphics produced by ggvis are fundamentally web graphics&quot;</i>.  More generally, it seems to be the future all-purpose package at the head of a family of web based plotting tools within htmlwidgets.  Another one of those is leaflet.  For now, there isn&#39;t a google group for either of those, and I&#39;m interested in a specific ggvis function - linked_brush - and I&#39;m wondering about it&#39;s potential portability to its brothers and sisters, in this case, leaflet.</div><div><br></div><div>Some people reading this may know both packages.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers and apologies.</div></div>"
    ],
